{
  "idea_units": [
    {
      "line_start": 128,
      "line_end": 128,
      "text": "The team is considering changing the format of short-term memory because tests showed it becomes too large and unwieldy.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 132,
      "line_end": 132,
      "text": "A critique of tree-based memory structures is that by breaking up memories, they lose the temporal dimension, which prevents implementing time-based weight decay.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 133,
      "line_end": 135,
      "text": "A proposal was made for long-term memory to use a time-ordered structure instead of a tree. Retrieval would be based on semantic similarity plus a \"Recency\" score that decays over time, but with a \"floor\" to prevent important old memories from disappearing.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 136,
      "line_end": 137,
      "text": "The goal of the proposed memory model is to create a trade-off where older, less relevant information fades, while crucial past events can still be retrieved, contrasting with models that aim for perfect recall.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    },
    {
      "line_start": 138,
      "line_end": 140,
      "text": "The team is looking for existing models or papers about retrieval that considers both importance and time decay. \"WebCAG\" was suggested as a possible reference, but an initial search was inconclusive.",
      "completeness": "complete",
      "uncertainty_note": ""
    }
  ]
}

